event: response.output_text.done
data: {"type":"response.output_text.done","content_index":0,"item_id":"msg_014ad5a681765dc9016aa3e748bfa087d2afcd55daab953c60","logprobs":[],"output_index":1,"sequence_number":6434,"text":"openapi: 3.1.0\ninfo:\n  title: CardDemo Batch Transaction Boundary\n  version: 1.0.0\n  description: |\n    Contract for individual invocations of CBTRN02C (posting), CBACT04C\n    (interest generation), and CBTRN03C (reporting), not for an entire batch\n    schedule.\n\n    HTTP paths, synchronous POST requests, JSON envelopes, dataset binding\n    identifiers, base64 record transport, and HTTP status codes are chosen\n    transport conventions. They are not interfaces implemented by the COBOL\n    sources. A dataset binding identifies an already provisioned file in the\n    execution environment; it does not create or validate its contents.\n\n    Sequential input records are supplied in order. Persistent indexed files\n    are accessed through bindings with the access modes described per operation.\n    Output arrays expose logical records written by the program, without\n    sequential-file block headers or record framing. They do not imply that\n    output files or writes are transactional. Missing keys, duplicate transaction\n    identifiers, arbitrary alphanumeric dates and card numbers, empty files,\n    and malformed numeric storage remain representable.\n\n    All three programs display diagnostics and call CEE3ABD with code 999 and\n    timing 0 on their explicit abend paths. Availability and actual behavior of\n    that external routine are not established by the corpus. No atomicity,\n    rollback, retry, idempotency, locking, or automatic recovery is promised.\n    Earlier writes and output-file initialization may persist after failure.\nx-uncertainties:\n  - The corpus supplies no HTTP server, runtime deployment, encoding configuration, or proof that the referenced datasets and utilities are available.\n  - Raw records use the execution environment's COBOL display encoding, including signed display numeric representation. This contract does not prescribe ASCII, EBCDIC, or a sign-overpunch translation.\n  - COBOL arithmetic has fixed receiving-field sizes and no ON SIZE ERROR handling here. Overflow and malformed numeric data are not converted into invented business rejections.\n  - SORT, IDCAMS, CEE3ABD, and the REPROCT control member are not supplied implementations. JCL references do not establish their execution.\n  - TRANBKP describes backup, deletion, and redefinition of the transaction master. COMBTRAN describes sorting backup plus system transactions by ID and loading the master. Neither is implicitly executed by these operations.\n  - TRANREPT JCL describes external unload, date filtering, and card-number sorting. These steps are not implicitly executed by the reporting operation; the JCL also repeats the STEP05R step name.\npaths:\n  /transaction-postings:\n    post:\n      operationId: postDailyTransactions\n      summary: Run daily transaction posting\n      description: |\n        Executes the observable boundary of CBTRN02C. DALYTRAN is read\n        sequentially; XREFFILE is input; ACCTFILE and TCATBALF are I-O.\n        TRANFILE is indexed with a 16-byte transaction-ID key and is opened\n        OUTPUT, not I-O or EXTEND. DALYREJS is opened OUTPUT. This is not an\n        append-to-existing-master promise; output initialization can replace\n        existing content according to the runtime.\n\n        Each successfully read daily record increments the processed counter.\n        Validation first reads the card cross-reference. INVALID KEY gives\n        0100, INVALID CARD NUMBER FOUND. Only if that succeeds is the account\n        read; INVALID KEY gives 0101, ACCOUNT RECORD NOT FOUND. With an account,\n        a signed nine-integer-digit, two-decimal temporary value is computed as\n        currentCycleCredit - currentCycleDebit + dailyAmount. A value greater\n        than creditLimit gives 0102, OVERLIMIT TRANSACTION. Then expirationDate\n        is compared as PIC X(10) to the first ten characters of originalTimestamp.\n        If expirationDate is less, 0103, TRANSACTION RECEIVED AFTER ACCT\n        EXPIRATION, overwrites 0102. Equality passes both comparisons.\n\n        A rejected record is copied unchanged, including its processing timestamp\n        and filler, to a 430-byte rejection record with a four-digit reason and\n        a space-padded 76-character message. Processing continues. Rejected\n        records do not take the posting branch. A completed run with any\n        rejections explicitly sets RETURN-CODE to 4. The no-rejection branch\n        does not explicitly assign RETURN-CODE.\n\n        Posting copies all named transaction fields except processingTimestamp,\n        which is replaced by the runtime current timestamp. Filler is not copied\n        or initialized explicitly. Effects occur in this order:\n        (1) read category balance by account, type, category; on status 23 create\n        an initialized balance record containing the amount, otherwise add the\n        amount and rewrite;\n        (2) add amount to account currentBalance; if amount >= 0 add it to\n        currentCycleCredit, otherwise add the negative amount to\n        currentCycleDebit; rewrite the account;\n        (3) write the indexed transaction record.\n\n        Account rewrite INVALID KEY sets internal reason 0109, ACCOUNT RECORD\n        NOT FOUND, but that value is not retested for rejection and does not\n        increment the reject counter. The transaction write is still attempted.\n        No separate 0109 rejection response is promised. Other statuses on\n        validation lookups and account rewrite are not comprehensively checked.\n\n        Checked open/close failures, daily read statuses other than 00/10,\n        category read statuses other than 00/23, category write/rewrite failures,\n        rejection writes, and transaction writes lead to the explicit abend path.\n        A duplicate transaction key can fail the final write after balance\n        changes; there is no duplicate prevalidation. No card-number digit or\n        checksum validation, account-active validation, cash-limit validation,\n        transaction type/category lookup, positivity restriction, or calendar\n        validation is present.\n      x-preconditions:\n        - Bound files must be provisioned in the environment with the declared organization and access permissions.\n        - XREFFILE uses the 16-byte card key; ACCTFILE uses the 11-digit account key; TCATBALF uses the 17-byte account/type/category key.\n        - Input order is significant because accepted records update balances used by later records.\n      requestBody:\n        required: true\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              type: object\n              additionalProperties: false\n              required:\n                - dailyTransactions\n                - cardCrossReference\n                - accounts\n                - categoryBalances\n                - transactionOutput\n                - rejectionOutput\n              properties:\n                dailyTransactions:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/TransactionRecords'\n                cardCrossReference:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n                accounts:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n                categoryBalances:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n                transactionOutput:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n                rejectionOutput:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: Completed invocation, including completion with business rejections.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                allOf:\n                  - $ref: '#/components/schemas/CompletedRun'\n                  - type: object\n                    required: [processedCount, rejectedCount, transactionsWritten, rejections]\n                    properties:\n                      processedCount:\n                        $ref: '#/components/schemas/Counter'\n                      rejectedCount:\n                        $ref: '#/components/schemas/Counter'\n                      transactionsWritten:\n                        $ref: '#/components/schemas/TransactionRecords'\n                      rejections:\n                        type: array\n                        items:\n                          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Rejection'\n        '500':\n          $ref: '#/components/responses/ExecutionFailure'\n  /interest-transaction-generations:\n    post:\n      operationId: generateInterestTransactions\n      summary: Generate system interest transactions from category balances\n      description: |\n        Executes CBACT04C independently of posting and master-combination jobs.\n        TCATBALF is indexed sequential input in account/type/category key order.\n        XREFFILE and DISCGRP are random input, ACCTFILE is random I-O, and\n        TRANSACT is sequential OUTPUT. No indexed transaction master is written.\n\n        On each account change, the prior account is rewritten, except before\n        the first account. The program then resets its accumulated interest,\n        reads the new account, and reads the cross-reference using the alternate\n        account-ID key. It uses the returned card number, not a caller-selected\n        card. Account or cross-reference read failure abends.\n\n        For every category balance it reads the disclosure rate using the account\n        group, balance type, and balance category. Status 23 causes another read\n        with group DEFAULT padded to ten characters, retaining type and category.\n        Failure of that default read abends; other nonzero initial read statuses\n        except 23 also abend.\n\n        When rate is nonzero, monthlyInterest = balance * rate / 1200 is assigned\n        to PIC S9(09)V99 without ROUNDED, and added to a same-sized account\n        accumulator. One transaction is written even if the calculated interest\n        is zero or negative. A zero rate writes no transaction. Fee calculation\n        is a no-op.\n\n        The transaction ID is the ten-character parameter followed by a six-digit\n        counter starting at 000001, incremented for each generated transaction.\n        The parameter length field is not inspected and the parameter is not\n        validated as a date. Type is 01, numeric category is 0005, source is\n        System padded to ten characters, description begins 'Int. for a/c '\n        followed by the eleven-digit account ID, amount is monthlyInterest,\n        merchant ID is zero, and merchant name/city/ZIP are spaces.\n        Both timestamps are runtime current timestamps. Transaction working\n        storage is not initialized per write; description tail and filler are\n        not explicitly assigned.\n\n        Updating an account adds accumulated interest to currentBalance and\n        sets both cycle credit and cycle debit to zero. Critically, the source\n        performs this update on transition to another account only. The ELSE\n        intended to update at EOF is unreachable under the loop condition:\n        EOF is set by the read while already inside the other branch. Consequently\n        the final account is not rewritten, even though its generated\n        transactions may be written. An empty balance file rewrites no accounts.\n        Category balances are input-only and are not cleared or updated.\n\n        Checked open/close, sequential read other than EOF, lookup, account\n        rewrite, and transaction write failures invoke the abend path. Generated\n        transactions are not automatically posted, merged, or loaded.\n      x-preconditions:\n        - TCATBALF must support sequential indexed-key traversal.\n        - XREFFILE must support the account-ID alternate-key read used by this program.\n        - INTCALC JCL references XREFFIL1 as an alternate-index path, but availability and association of that infrastructure are not established.\n      x-uncertainties:\n        - Behavior of six-digit transaction suffix overflow is not handled explicitly; generated IDs are not checked for collisions.\n        - Multiple cross-reference rows for an account and runtime alternate-index behavior are not resolved by the supplied source.\n      requestBody:\n        required: true\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              type: object\n              additionalProperties: false\n              required:\n                - transactionIdPrefix\n                - categoryBalances\n                - cardCrossReference\n                - accounts\n                - disclosureGroups\n                - transactionOutput\n              properties:\n                transactionIdPrefix:\n                  type: string\n                  minLength: 10\n                  maxLength: 10\n                  description: |\n                    Exact PIC X(10) linkage parameter, mapped to ten execution-encoding\n                    bytes. Not an ISO date. INTCALC supplies 2022071800.\n                  examples: ['2022071800', 'XXXXXXXXXX']\n                categoryBalances:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n                cardCrossReference:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n                accounts:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n                disclosureGroups:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n                transactionOutput:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: |\n            Completed generation. Account rewrites are limited to account\n            transitions as described, not all accounts represented in output.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                allOf:\n                  - $ref: '#/components/schemas/CompletedRun'\n                  - type: object\n                    required: [transactionsWritten]\n                    properties:\n                      transactionsWritten:\n                        $ref: '#/components/schemas/TransactionRecords'\n        '500':\n          $ref: '#/components/responses/ExecutionFailure'\n  /transaction-reports:\n    post:\n      operationId: generateTransactionReport\n      summary: Produce the fixed-width daily transaction detail report\n      description: |\n        Executes CBTRN03C against the supplied sequential transaction stream.\n        CARDXREF, TRANTYPE, and TRANCATG are indexed random input. TRANREPT is\n        sequential OUTPUT. This operation changes no input master records.\n\n        Only the first DATEPARM record is read: positions 1-10 are startDate,\n        position 11 is ignored, and positions 12-21 are endDate. Remaining bytes\n        and subsequent records are ignored. An empty DATEPARM file sets EOF and\n        skips transaction processing, leaving the opened output without report\n        records. Dates are unvalidated PIC X(10); no start-before-end validation\n        is performed.\n\n        The first ten characters of processingTimestamp are compared inclusively\n        against the date parameters. A failed comparison uses NEXT SENTENCE,\n        skipping the remainder of the main processing sentence for that iteration.\n        Records are neither sorted nor regrouped internally.\n\n        On a change of card number among included records, a prior 'Account Total'\n        is printed if details have begun, then the new card cross-reference is\n        read. Thus grouping is by contiguous card, not by account ID. Each included\n        record looks up its type and its type/category pair. INVALID KEY on these\n        three lookups displays the offending key, reports status 23, and abends.\n        Other lookup statuses are not comprehensively checked. Blank initial card\n        numbers can bypass the first cross-reference lookup because the current\n        card working field initially contains spaces.\n\n        The first detail causes four header lines. Before each detail, a page\n        break is considered only if lineCounter MOD 20 = 0. The counter includes\n        headers, details, totals and separator lines; it is not reset per page.\n        A page-total routine writes its total and a hyphen separator, adds the\n        page total to the grand total, resets the page total, and increments\n        the counter twice. An account-total routine writes its total and a\n        separator, resets the account total, and also increments it twice.\n\n        At transaction EOF the program still evaluates the date condition on\n        transaction working storage. If that condition passes, the EOF branch\n        adds TRAN-AMT again to page and account accumulators, writes page totals,\n        then grand totals. It does not write the final account total. With the\n        usual retained last record this double-counts the last amount in final\n        page/grand totals. If the retained last record is out of range, NEXT\n        SENTENCE skips final totals. Empty transaction input leaves these tests\n        dependent on uninitialized transaction storage. This contract does not\n        substitute corrected totals or guarantee an empty-input grand-total line.\n\n        Checked open/close failures, transaction/date reads other than 00/10,\n        report writes, and invalid lookup keys take the explicit abend path.\n      x-preconditions:\n        - The caller must provide the desired sequential stream; contiguous card ordering is needed for consolidated card subtotals but is not validated or enforced.\n        - External JCL filtering uses independently hard-coded dates 2022-01-01 through 2022-07-06 and sorts the card field as ZD. Those constraints are not restrictions on this program-level input.\n      requestBody:\n        required: true\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              type: object\n              additionalProperties: false\n              required:\n                - transactions\n                - dateParameterRecords\n                - cardCrossReference\n                - transactionTypes\n                - transactionCategories\n                - reportOutput\n              properties:\n                transactions:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/TransactionRecords'\n                dateParameterRecords:\n                  type: array\n                  description: Empty is permitted; only the first record is read.\n                  items:\n                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/DateParameterRecord'\n                cardCrossReference:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n                transactionTypes:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n                transactionCategories:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n                reportOutput:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: Completed report, preserving the source formatting and control-flow behavior.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                allOf:\n                  - $ref: '#/components/schemas/CompletedRun'\n                  - type: object\n                    required: [reportRecords]\n                    properties:\n                      reportRecords:\n                        type: array\n                        items:\n                          $ref: '#/components/schemas/ReportRecord'\n        '500':\n          $ref: '#/components/responses/ExecutionFailure'\ncomponents:\n  responses:\n    ExecutionFailure:\n      description: |\n        Transport convention for an invocation that does not complete normally.\n        This is distinct from a posting business rejection. Diagnostics and\n        partial output are exposed only if recoverable from the execution\n        environment. No reversal of output initialization or earlier writes is\n        implied. A close failure can occur after all record effects.\n      content:\n        application/json:\n          schema:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/FailedRun'\n  schemas:\n    DatasetBinding:\n      type: string\n      minLength: 1\n      description: |\n        Opaque transport identifier for a pre-existing runtime file binding.\n        Missing, inaccessible, incorrectly organized, or incorrectly provisioned\n        resources are execution failures, not exclusions from this schema.\n        No public dataset-management operation is defined.\n    Counter:\n      type: integer\n      minimum: 0\n      maximum: 999999999\n      description: Value of the program's nine-digit counter, not an unlimited count.\n    CompletedRun:\n      type: object\n      required: [outcome, diagnostics]\n      properties:\n        outcome:\n          const: completed\n        returnCode:\n          type: integer\n          description: |\n            Runtime return code if available. Posting explicitly sets 4 when\n            any records were rejected; otherwise these programs do not explicitly\n            establish a success return code.\n        diagnostics:\n          type: array\n          items:\n            type: string\n          description: DISPLAY output in execution order, decoded by the environment.\n    FailedRun:\n      type: object\n      required: [outcome, diagnostics]\n      properties:\n        outcome:\n          const: failed\n        program:\n          type: string\n          enum: [CBTRN02C, CBACT04C, CBTRN03C]\n        diagnostics:\n          type: array\n          items:\n            type: string\n        abendCode:\n          type: integer\n          const: 999\n          description: Present when the explicit CEE3ABD request is observed.\n        fileStatus:\n          type: string\n          description: |\n            Observed file-status diagnostic, when available; not normalized into\n            a business error. The programs expand nonnumeric or 9-prefixed status\n            values using a binary second byte. Posting's rejection-file close\n            failure mistakenly displays XREFFILE status.\n        partialTransactions:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/TransactionRecords'\n        partialRejections:\n          type: array\n          items:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/Rejection'\n        partialReportRecords:\n          type: array\n          items:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/ReportRecord'\n        effectsDescription:\n          type: string\n          description: Observed effects only; omission does not establish that no writes persisted.\n    TransactionRecords:\n      type: array\n      description: |\n        Logical 350-byte records in input or write order. Empty arrays, repeated\n        identifiers, nonnumeric card numbers, arbitrary timestamps, negative\n        amounts and raw malformed numeric storage are representable.\n      items:\n        $ref: '#/components/schemas/TransactionRecord'\n    TransactionRecord:\n      type: string\n      contentEncoding: base64\n      contentMediaType: application/octet-stream\n      x-decoded-byte-length: 350\n      description: |\n        Exactly 350 decoded bytes, CVTRA05Y or CVTRA06Y. Widths and offsets\n        below are one-based, in bytes, with no delimiters. Raw transport retains\n        filler and invalid display-numeric bytes rather than introducing\n        unsupported field validation. Numeric pictures describe intended storage,\n        not business admissibility. Signed values use the runtime display sign\n        representation, without an extra sign byte. V is an implied decimal.\n\n        Named fields on accepted postings are copied except processingTimestamp;\n        rejection output preserves the entire original record. Runtime-generated\n        timestamps have the form YYYY-MM-DD-HH.MM.SS.hh0000, with hundredths from\n        CURRENT-DATE and no timezone suffix; they are not RFC 3339.\n      x-record-layout:\n        - {name: transactionId, offset: 1, length: 16, picture: 'X(16)'}\n        - {name: typeCode, offset: 17, length: 2, picture: 'X(02)'}\n        - {name: categoryCode, offset: 19, length: 4, picture: '9(04)'}\n        - {name: source, offset: 23, length: 10, picture: 'X(10)'}\n        - {name: description, offset: 33, length: 100, picture: 'X(100)'}\n        - {name: amount, offset: 133, length: 11, picture: 'S9(09)V99', nominalRange: '-999999999.99 to 999999999.99'}\n        - {name: merchantId, offset: 144, length: 9, picture: '9(09)'}\n        - {name: merchantName, offset: 153, length: 50, picture: 'X(50)'}\n        - {name: merchantCity, offset: 203, length: 50, picture: 'X(50)'}\n        - {name: merchantZip, offset: 253, length: 10, picture: 'X(10)'}\n        - {name: cardNumber, offset: 263, length: 16, picture: 'X(16)'}\n        - {name: originalTimestamp, offset: 279, length: 26, picture: 'X(26)'}\n        - {name: processingTimestamp, offset: 305, length: 26, picture: 'X(26)'}\n        - {name: filler, offset: 331, length: 20, picture: 'X(20)'}\n    Rejection:\n      type: object\n      required: [record, reasonCode, reasonDescription]\n      properties:\n        record:\n          type: string\n          contentEncoding: base64\n          contentMediaType: application/octet-stream\n          x-decoded-byte-length: 430\n          description: |\n            Original 350-byte daily transaction followed by PIC 9(04) reason\n            and PIC X(76) description, space-padded.\n        reasonCode:\n          type: string\n          enum: ['0100', '0101', '0102', '0103']\n        reasonDescription:\n          type: string\n          enum:\n            - INVALID CARD NUMBER FOUND\n            - ACCOUNT RECORD NOT FOUND\n            - OVERLIMIT TRANSACTION\n            - TRANSACTION RECEIVED AFTER ACCT EXPIRATION\n      description: Decoded reason fields are transport projections of the raw trailer, with trailing message spaces removed.\n    DateParameterRecord:\n      type: string\n      contentEncoding: base64\n      contentMediaType: application/octet-stream\n      x-decoded-byte-length: 80\n      description: |\n        Exactly 80 decoded bytes. Start date is bytes 1-10, byte 11 is ignored,\n        end date is bytes 12-21, bytes 22-80 are ignored. Arbitrary character\n        content, reversed ranges, and spaces are representable; there is no\n        calendar or separator validation.\n    ReportRecord:\n      type: string\n      contentEncoding: base64\n      contentMediaType: application/octet-stream\n      x-decoded-byte-length: 133\n      description: |\n        Exactly 133 decoded bytes, including trailing spaces. CVTRA07Y headers\n        name DALYREPT and Daily Transaction Report and contain Date Range with\n        the supplied start/end strings. Detail columns contain transaction ID\n        (16), space, account ID (11), space, type (2), hyphen, type description\n        truncated to 15, space, category (4), hyphen, category description\n        truncated to 29, space, source (10), four spaces, amount edited with\n        PIC -ZZZ,ZZZ,ZZZ.ZZ, and two spaces, then padding to 133.\n        Separators contain 133 hyphens. Page Total, Account Total and Grand\n        Total lines have dotted leaders and PIC +ZZZ,ZZZ,ZZZ.ZZ values.\n        Report totals are source accumulators, not independently recomputed\n        or corrected API aggregates.\nx-persistent-record-layouts:\n  description: |\n    Layout evidence for datasets referenced by DatasetBinding. These are not\n    new provisioning or maintenance APIs. Keys retain leading zeros and fixed\n    character padding. No foreign-key completeness or business-domain enumeration\n    is imposed on bound data.\n  accounts:\n    source: CVACT01Y\n    length: 300\n    key: [accountId]\n    fields:\n      - {name: accountId, picture: '9(11)', length: 11}\n      - {name: activeStatus, picture: 'X(01)', length: 1}\n      - {name: currentBalance, picture: 'S9(10)V99', length: 12}\n      - {name: creditLimit, picture: 'S9(10)V99', length: 12}\n      - {name: cashCreditLimit, picture: 'S9(10)V99', length: 12}\n      - {name: openDate, picture: 'X(10)', length: 10}\n      - {name: expirationDate, picture: 'X(10)', length: 10}\n      - {name: reissueDate, picture: 'X(10)', length: 10}\n      - {name: currentCycleCredit, picture: 'S9(10)V99', length: 12}\n      - {name: currentCycleDebit, picture: 'S9(10)V99', length: 12}\n      - {name: addressZip, picture: 'X(10)', length: 10}\n      - {name: groupId, picture: 'X(10)', length: 10}\n      - {name: filler, picture: 'X(178)', length: 178}\n  cardCrossReference:\n    source: CVACT03Y\n    length: 50\n    key: [cardNumber]\n    interestAlternateKey: [accountId]\n    fields:\n      - {name: cardNumber, picture: 'X(16)', length: 16}\n      - {name: customerId, picture: '9(09)', length: 9}\n      - {name: accountId, picture: '9(11)', length: 11}\n      - {name: filler, picture: 'X(14)', length: 14}\n  categoryBalances:\n    source: CVTRA01Y\n    length: 50\n    key: [accountId, typeCode, categoryCode]\n    fields:\n      - {name: accountId, picture: '9(11)', length: 11}\n      - {name: typeCode, picture: 'X(02)', length: 2}\n      - {name: categoryCode, picture: '9(04)', length: 4}\n      - {name: balance, picture: 'S9(09)V99', length: 11}\n      - {name: filler, picture: 'X(22)', length: 22}\n  disclosureGroups:\n    source: CVTRA02Y\n    length: 50\n    key: [groupId, typeCode, categoryCode]\n    fields:\n      - {name: groupId, picture: 'X(10)', length: 10}\n      - {name: typeCode, picture: 'X(02)', length: 2}\n      - {name: categoryCode, picture: '9(04)', length: 4}\n      - {name: interestRate, picture: 'S9(04)V99', length: 6}\n      - {name: filler, picture: 'X(28)', length: 28}\n  transactionTypes:\n    source: CVTRA03Y\n    length: 60\n    key: [typeCode]\n    fields:\n      - {name: typeCode, picture: 'X(02)', length: 2}\n      - {name: description, picture: 'X(50)', length: 50}\n      - {name: filler, picture: 'X(08)', length: 8}\n  transactionCategories:\n    source: CVTRA04Y\n    length: 60\n    key: [typeCode, categoryCode]\n    fields:\n      - {name: typeCode, picture: 'X(02)', length: 2}\n      - {name: categoryCode, picture: '9(04)', length: 4}\n      - {name: description, picture: 'X(50)', length: 50}\n      - {name: filler, picture: 'X(04)', length: 4}\n"}

event: response.content_part.done
data: {"type":"response.content_part.done","content_index":0,"item_id":"msg_014ad5a681765dc9016aa3e748bfa087d2afcd55daab953c60","output_index":1,"part":{"type":"output_text","annotations":[],"logprobs":[],"text":"openapi: 3.1.0\ninfo:\n  title: CardDemo Batch Transaction Boundary\n  version: 1.0.0\n  description: |\n    Contract for individual invocations of CBTRN02C (posting), CBACT04C\n    (interest generation), and CBTRN03C (reporting), not for an entire batch\n    schedule.\n\n    HTTP paths, synchronous POST requests, JSON envelopes, dataset binding\n    identifiers, base64 record transport, and HTTP status codes are chosen\n    transport conventions. They are not interfaces implemented by the COBOL\n    sources. A dataset binding identifies an already provisioned file in the\n    execution environment; it does not create or validate its contents.\n\n    Sequential input records are supplied in order. Persistent indexed files\n    are accessed through bindings with the access modes described per operation.\n    Output arrays expose logical records written by the program, without\n    sequential-file block headers or record framing. They do not imply that\n    output files or writes are transactional. Missing keys, duplicate transaction\n    identifiers, arbitrary alphanumeric dates and card numbers, empty files,\n    and malformed numeric storage remain representable.\n\n    All three programs display diagnostics and call CEE3ABD with code 999 and\n    timing 0 on their explicit abend paths. Availability and actual behavior of\n    that external routine are not established by the corpus. No atomicity,\n    rollback, retry, idempotency, locking, or automatic recovery is promised.\n    Earlier writes and output-file initialization may persist after failure.\nx-uncertainties:\n  - The corpus supplies no HTTP server, runtime deployment, encoding configuration, or proof that the referenced datasets and utilities are available.\n  - Raw records use the execution environment's COBOL display encoding, including signed display numeric representation. This contract does not prescribe ASCII, EBCDIC, or a sign-overpunch translation.\n  - COBOL arithmetic has fixed receiving-field sizes and no ON SIZE ERROR handling here. Overflow and malformed numeric data are not converted into invented business rejections.\n  - SORT, IDCAMS, CEE3ABD, and the REPROCT control member are not supplied implementations. JCL references do not establish their execution.\n  - TRANBKP describes backup, deletion, and redefinition of the transaction master. COMBTRAN describes sorting backup plus system transactions by ID and loading the master. Neither is implicitly executed by these operations.\n  - TRANREPT JCL describes external unload, date filtering, and card-number sorting. These steps are not implicitly executed by the reporting operation; the JCL also repeats the STEP05R step name.\npaths:\n  /transaction-postings:\n    post:\n      operationId: postDailyTransactions\n      summary: Run daily transaction posting\n      description: |\n        Executes the observable boundary of CBTRN02C. DALYTRAN is read\n        sequentially; XREFFILE is input; ACCTFILE and TCATBALF are I-O.\n        TRANFILE is indexed with a 16-byte transaction-ID key and is opened\n        OUTPUT, not I-O or EXTEND. DALYREJS is opened OUTPUT. This is not an\n        append-to-existing-master promise; output initialization can replace\n        existing content according to the runtime.\n\n        Each successfully read daily record increments the processed counter.\n        Validation first reads the card cross-reference. INVALID KEY gives\n        0100, INVALID CARD NUMBER FOUND. Only if that succeeds is the account\n        read; INVALID KEY gives 0101, ACCOUNT RECORD NOT FOUND. With an account,\n        a signed nine-integer-digit, two-decimal temporary value is computed as\n        currentCycleCredit - currentCycleDebit + dailyAmount. A value greater\n        than creditLimit gives 0102, OVERLIMIT TRANSACTION. Then expirationDate\n        is compared as PIC X(10) to the first ten characters of originalTimestamp.\n        If expirationDate is less, 0103, TRANSACTION RECEIVED AFTER ACCT\n        EXPIRATION, overwrites 0102. Equality passes both comparisons.\n\n        A rejected record is copied unchanged, including its processing timestamp\n        and filler, to a 430-byte rejection record with a four-digit reason and\n        a space-padded 76-character message. Processing continues. Rejected\n        records do not take the posting branch. A completed run with any\n        rejections explicitly sets RETURN-CODE to 4. The no-rejection branch\n        does not explicitly assign RETURN-CODE.\n\n        Posting copies all named transaction fields except processingTimestamp,\n        which is replaced by the runtime current timestamp. Filler is not copied\n        or initialized explicitly. Effects occur in this order:\n        (1) read category balance by account, type, category; on status 23 create\n        an initialized balance record containing the amount, otherwise add the\n        amount and rewrite;\n        (2) add amount to account currentBalance; if amount >= 0 add it to\n        currentCycleCredit, otherwise add the negative amount to\n        currentCycleDebit; rewrite the account;\n        (3) write the indexed transaction record.\n\n        Account rewrite INVALID KEY sets internal reason 0109, ACCOUNT RECORD\n        NOT FOUND, but that value is not retested for rejection and does not\n        increment the reject counter. The transaction write is still attempted.\n        No separate 0109 rejection response is promised. Other statuses on\n        validation lookups and account rewrite are not comprehensively checked.\n\n        Checked open/close failures, daily read statuses other than 00/10,\n        category read statuses other than 00/23, category write/rewrite failures,\n        rejection writes, and transaction writes lead to the explicit abend path.\n        A duplicate transaction key can fail the final write after balance\n        changes; there is no duplicate prevalidation. No card-number digit or\n        checksum validation, account-active validation, cash-limit validation,\n        transaction type/category lookup, positivity restriction, or calendar\n        validation is present.\n      x-preconditions:\n        - Bound files must be provisioned in the environment with the declared organization and access permissions.\n        - XREFFILE uses the 16-byte card key; ACCTFILE uses the 11-digit account key; TCATBALF uses the 17-byte account/type/category key.\n        - Input order is significant because accepted records update balances used by later records.\n      requestBody:\n        required: true\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              type: object\n              additionalProperties: false\n              required:\n                - dailyTransactions\n                - cardCrossReference\n                - accounts\n                - categoryBalances\n                - transactionOutput\n                - rejectionOutput\n              properties:\n                dailyTransactions:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/TransactionRecords'\n                cardCrossReference:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n                accounts:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n                categoryBalances:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n                transactionOutput:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n                rejectionOutput:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: Completed invocation, including completion with business rejections.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                allOf:\n                  - $ref: '#/components/schemas/CompletedRun'\n                  - type: object\n                    required: [processedCount, rejectedCount, transactionsWritten, rejections]\n                    properties:\n                      processedCount:\n                        $ref: '#/components/schemas/Counter'\n                      rejectedCount:\n                        $ref: '#/components/schemas/Counter'\n                      transactionsWritten:\n                        $ref: '#/components/schemas/TransactionRecords'\n                      rejections:\n                        type: array\n                        items:\n                          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Rejection'\n        '500':\n          $ref: '#/components/responses/ExecutionFailure'\n  /interest-transaction-generations:\n    post:\n      operationId: generateInterestTransactions\n      summary: Generate system interest transactions from category balances\n      description: |\n        Executes CBACT04C independently of posting and master-combination jobs.\n        TCATBALF is indexed sequential input in account/type/category key order.\n        XREFFILE and DISCGRP are random input, ACCTFILE is random I-O, and\n        TRANSACT is sequential OUTPUT. No indexed transaction master is written.\n\n        On each account change, the prior account is rewritten, except before\n        the first account. The program then resets its accumulated interest,\n        reads the new account, and reads the cross-reference using the alternate\n        account-ID key. It uses the returned card number, not a caller-selected\n        card. Account or cross-reference read failure abends.\n\n        For every category balance it reads the disclosure rate using the account\n        group, balance type, and balance category. Status 23 causes another read\n        with group DEFAULT padded to ten characters, retaining type and category.\n        Failure of that default read abends; other nonzero initial read statuses\n        except 23 also abend.\n\n        When rate is nonzero, monthlyInterest = balance * rate / 1200 is assigned\n        to PIC S9(09)V99 without ROUNDED, and added to a same-sized account\n        accumulator. One transaction is written even if the calculated interest\n        is zero or negative. A zero rate writes no transaction. Fee calculation\n        is a no-op.\n\n        The transaction ID is the ten-character parameter followed by a six-digit\n        counter starting at 000001, incremented for each generated transaction.\n        The parameter length field is not inspected and the parameter is not\n        validated as a date. Type is 01, numeric category is 0005, source is\n        System padded to ten characters, description begins 'Int. for a/c '\n        followed by the eleven-digit account ID, amount is monthlyInterest,\n        merchant ID is zero, and merchant name/city/ZIP are spaces.\n        Both timestamps are runtime current timestamps. Transaction working\n        storage is not initialized per write; description tail and filler are\n        not explicitly assigned.\n\n        Updating an account adds accumulated interest to currentBalance and\n        sets both cycle credit and cycle debit to zero. Critically, the source\n        performs this update on transition to another account only. The ELSE\n        intended to update at EOF is unreachable under the loop condition:\n        EOF is set by the read while already inside the other branch. Consequently\n        the final account is not rewritten, even though its generated\n        transactions may be written. An empty balance file rewrites no accounts.\n        Category balances are input-only and are not cleared or updated.\n\n        Checked open/close, sequential read other than EOF, lookup, account\n        rewrite, and transaction write failures invoke the abend path. Generated\n        transactions are not automatically posted, merged, or loaded.\n      x-preconditions:\n        - TCATBALF must support sequential indexed-key traversal.\n        - XREFFILE must support the account-ID alternate-key read used by this program.\n        - INTCALC JCL references XREFFIL1 as an alternate-index path, but availability and association of that infrastructure are not established.\n      x-uncertainties:\n        - Behavior of six-digit transaction suffix overflow is not handled explicitly; generated IDs are not checked for collisions.\n        - Multiple cross-reference rows for an account and runtime alternate-index behavior are not resolved by the supplied source.\n      requestBody:\n        required: true\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              type: object\n              additionalProperties: false\n              required:\n                - transactionIdPrefix\n                - categoryBalances\n                - cardCrossReference\n                - accounts\n                - disclosureGroups\n                - transactionOutput\n              properties:\n                transactionIdPrefix:\n                  type: string\n                  minLength: 10\n                  maxLength: 10\n                  description: |\n                    Exact PIC X(10) linkage parameter, mapped to ten execution-encoding\n                    bytes. Not an ISO date. INTCALC supplies 2022071800.\n                  examples: ['2022071800', 'XXXXXXXXXX']\n                categoryBalances:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n                cardCrossReference:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n                accounts:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n                disclosureGroups:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n                transactionOutput:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: |\n            Completed generation. Account rewrites are limited to account\n            transitions as described, not all accounts represented in output.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                allOf:\n                  - $ref: '#/components/schemas/CompletedRun'\n                  - type: object\n                    required: [transactionsWritten]\n                    properties:\n                      transactionsWritten:\n                        $ref: '#/components/schemas/TransactionRecords'\n        '500':\n          $ref: '#/components/responses/ExecutionFailure'\n  /transaction-reports:\n    post:\n      operationId: generateTransactionReport\n      summary: Produce the fixed-width daily transaction detail report\n      description: |\n        Executes CBTRN03C against the supplied sequential transaction stream.\n        CARDXREF, TRANTYPE, and TRANCATG are indexed random input. TRANREPT is\n        sequential OUTPUT. This operation changes no input master records.\n\n        Only the first DATEPARM record is read: positions 1-10 are startDate,\n        position 11 is ignored, and positions 12-21 are endDate. Remaining bytes\n        and subsequent records are ignored. An empty DATEPARM file sets EOF and\n        skips transaction processing, leaving the opened output without report\n        records. Dates are unvalidated PIC X(10); no start-before-end validation\n        is performed.\n\n        The first ten characters of processingTimestamp are compared inclusively\n        against the date parameters. A failed comparison uses NEXT SENTENCE,\n        skipping the remainder of the main processing sentence for that iteration.\n        Records are neither sorted nor regrouped internally.\n\n        On a change of card number among included records, a prior 'Account Total'\n        is printed if details have begun, then the new card cross-reference is\n        read. Thus grouping is by contiguous card, not by account ID. Each included\n        record looks up its type and its type/category pair. INVALID KEY on these\n        three lookups displays the offending key, reports status 23, and abends.\n        Other lookup statuses are not comprehensively checked. Blank initial card\n        numbers can bypass the first cross-reference lookup because the current\n        card working field initially contains spaces.\n\n        The first detail causes four header lines. Before each detail, a page\n        break is considered only if lineCounter MOD 20 = 0. The counter includes\n        headers, details, totals and separator lines; it is not reset per page.\n        A page-total routine writes its total and a hyphen separator, adds the\n        page total to the grand total, resets the page total, and increments\n        the counter twice. An account-total routine writes its total and a\n        separator, resets the account total, and also increments it twice.\n\n        At transaction EOF the program still evaluates the date condition on\n        transaction working storage. If that condition passes, the EOF branch\n        adds TRAN-AMT again to page and account accumulators, writes page totals,\n        then grand totals. It does not write the final account total. With the\n        usual retained last record this double-counts the last amount in final\n        page/grand totals. If the retained last record is out of range, NEXT\n        SENTENCE skips final totals. Empty transaction input leaves these tests\n        dependent on uninitialized transaction storage. This contract does not\n        substitute corrected totals or guarantee an empty-input grand-total line.\n\n        Checked open/close failures, transaction/date reads other than 00/10,\n        report writes, and invalid lookup keys take the explicit abend path.\n      x-preconditions:\n        - The caller must provide the desired sequential stream; contiguous card ordering is needed for consolidated card subtotals but is not validated or enforced.\n        - External JCL filtering uses independently hard-coded dates 2022-01-01 through 2022-07-06 and sorts the card field as ZD. Those constraints are not restrictions on this program-level input.\n      requestBody:\n        required: true\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              type: object\n              additionalProperties: false\n              required:\n                - transactions\n                - dateParameterRecords\n                - cardCrossReference\n                - transactionTypes\n                - transactionCategories\n                - reportOutput\n              properties:\n                transactions:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/TransactionRecords'\n                dateParameterRecords:\n                  type: array\n                  description: Empty is permitted; only the first record is read.\n                  items:\n                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/DateParameterRecord'\n                cardCrossReference:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n                transactionTypes:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n                transactionCategories:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n                reportOutput:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: Completed report, preserving the source formatting and control-flow behavior.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                allOf:\n                  - $ref: '#/components/schemas/CompletedRun'\n                  - type: object\n                    required: [reportRecords]\n                    properties:\n                      reportRecords:\n                        type: array\n                        items:\n                          $ref: '#/components/schemas/ReportRecord'\n        '500':\n          $ref: '#/components/responses/ExecutionFailure'\ncomponents:\n  responses:\n    ExecutionFailure:\n      description: |\n        Transport convention for an invocation that does not complete normally.\n        This is distinct from a posting business rejection. Diagnostics and\n        partial output are exposed only if recoverable from the execution\n        environment. No reversal of output initialization or earlier writes is\n        implied. A close failure can occur after all record effects.\n      content:\n        application/json:\n          schema:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/FailedRun'\n  schemas:\n    DatasetBinding:\n      type: string\n      minLength: 1\n      description: |\n        Opaque transport identifier for a pre-existing runtime file binding.\n        Missing, inaccessible, incorrectly organized, or incorrectly provisioned\n        resources are execution failures, not exclusions from this schema.\n        No public dataset-management operation is defined.\n    Counter:\n      type: integer\n      minimum: 0\n      maximum: 999999999\n      description: Value of the program's nine-digit counter, not an unlimited count.\n    CompletedRun:\n      type: object\n      required: [outcome, diagnostics]\n      properties:\n        outcome:\n          const: completed\n        returnCode:\n          type: integer\n          description: |\n            Runtime return code if available. Posting explicitly sets 4 when\n            any records were rejected; otherwise these programs do not explicitly\n            establish a success return code.\n        diagnostics:\n          type: array\n          items:\n            type: string\n          description: DISPLAY output in execution order, decoded by the environment.\n    FailedRun:\n      type: object\n      required: [outcome, diagnostics]\n      properties:\n        outcome:\n          const: failed\n        program:\n          type: string\n          enum: [CBTRN02C, CBACT04C, CBTRN03C]\n        diagnostics:\n          type: array\n          items:\n            type: string\n        abendCode:\n          type: integer\n          const: 999\n          description: Present when the explicit CEE3ABD request is observed.\n        fileStatus:\n          type: string\n          description: |\n            Observed file-status diagnostic, when available; not normalized into\n            a business error. The programs expand nonnumeric or 9-prefixed status\n            values using a binary second byte. Posting's rejection-file close\n            failure mistakenly displays XREFFILE status.\n        partialTransactions:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/TransactionRecords'\n        partialRejections:\n          type: array\n          items:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/Rejection'\n        partialReportRecords:\n          type: array\n          items:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/ReportRecord'\n        effectsDescription:\n          type: string\n          description: Observed effects only; omission does not establish that no writes persisted.\n    TransactionRecords:\n      type: array\n      description: |\n        Logical 350-byte records in input or write order. Empty arrays, repeated\n        identifiers, nonnumeric card numbers, arbitrary timestamps, negative\n        amounts and raw malformed numeric storage are representable.\n      items:\n        $ref: '#/components/schemas/TransactionRecord'\n    TransactionRecord:\n      type: string\n      contentEncoding: base64\n      contentMediaType: application/octet-stream\n      x-decoded-byte-length: 350\n      description: |\n        Exactly 350 decoded bytes, CVTRA05Y or CVTRA06Y. Widths and offsets\n        below are one-based, in bytes, with no delimiters. Raw transport retains\n        filler and invalid display-numeric bytes rather than introducing\n        unsupported field validation. Numeric pictures describe intended storage,\n        not business admissibility. Signed values use the runtime display sign\n        representation, without an extra sign byte. V is an implied decimal.\n\n        Named fields on accepted postings are copied except processingTimestamp;\n        rejection output preserves the entire original record. Runtime-generated\n        timestamps have the form YYYY-MM-DD-HH.MM.SS.hh0000, with hundredths from\n        CURRENT-DATE and no timezone suffix; they are not RFC 3339.\n      x-record-layout:\n        - {name: transactionId, offset: 1, length: 16, picture: 'X(16)'}\n        - {name: typeCode, offset: 17, length: 2, picture: 'X(02)'}\n        - {name: categoryCode, offset: 19, length: 4, picture: '9(04)'}\n        - {name: source, offset: 23, length: 10, picture: 'X(10)'}\n        - {name: description, offset: 33, length: 100, picture: 'X(100)'}\n        - {name: amount, offset: 133, length: 11, picture: 'S9(09)V99', nominalRange: '-999999999.99 to 999999999.99'}\n        - {name: merchantId, offset: 144, length: 9, picture: '9(09)'}\n        - {name: merchantName, offset: 153, length: 50, picture: 'X(50)'}\n        - {name: merchantCity, offset: 203, length: 50, picture: 'X(50)'}\n        - {name: merchantZip, offset: 253, length: 10, picture: 'X(10)'}\n        - {name: cardNumber, offset: 263, length: 16, picture: 'X(16)'}\n        - {name: originalTimestamp, offset: 279, length: 26, picture: 'X(26)'}\n        - {name: processingTimestamp, offset: 305, length: 26, picture: 'X(26)'}\n        - {name: filler, offset: 331, length: 20, picture: 'X(20)'}\n    Rejection:\n      type: object\n      required: [record, reasonCode, reasonDescription]\n      properties:\n        record:\n          type: string\n          contentEncoding: base64\n          contentMediaType: application/octet-stream\n          x-decoded-byte-length: 430\n          description: |\n            Original 350-byte daily transaction followed by PIC 9(04) reason\n            and PIC X(76) description, space-padded.\n        reasonCode:\n          type: string\n          enum: ['0100', '0101', '0102', '0103']\n        reasonDescription:\n          type: string\n          enum:\n            - INVALID CARD NUMBER FOUND\n            - ACCOUNT RECORD NOT FOUND\n            - OVERLIMIT TRANSACTION\n            - TRANSACTION RECEIVED AFTER ACCT EXPIRATION\n      description: Decoded reason fields are transport projections of the raw trailer, with trailing message spaces removed.\n    DateParameterRecord:\n      type: string\n      contentEncoding: base64\n      contentMediaType: application/octet-stream\n      x-decoded-byte-length: 80\n      description: |\n        Exactly 80 decoded bytes. Start date is bytes 1-10, byte 11 is ignored,\n        end date is bytes 12-21, bytes 22-80 are ignored. Arbitrary character\n        content, reversed ranges, and spaces are representable; there is no\n        calendar or separator validation.\n    ReportRecord:\n      type: string\n      contentEncoding: base64\n      contentMediaType: application/octet-stream\n      x-decoded-byte-length: 133\n      description: |\n        Exactly 133 decoded bytes, including trailing spaces. CVTRA07Y headers\n        name DALYREPT and Daily Transaction Report and contain Date Range with\n        the supplied start/end strings. Detail columns contain transaction ID\n        (16), space, account ID (11), space, type (2), hyphen, type description\n        truncated to 15, space, category (4), hyphen, category description\n        truncated to 29, space, source (10), four spaces, amount edited with\n        PIC -ZZZ,ZZZ,ZZZ.ZZ, and two spaces, then padding to 133.\n        Separators contain 133 hyphens. Page Total, Account Total and Grand\n        Total lines have dotted leaders and PIC +ZZZ,ZZZ,ZZZ.ZZ values.\n        Report totals are source accumulators, not independently recomputed\n        or corrected API aggregates.\nx-persistent-record-layouts:\n  description: |\n    Layout evidence for datasets referenced by DatasetBinding. These are not\n    new provisioning or maintenance APIs. Keys retain leading zeros and fixed\n    character padding. No foreign-key completeness or business-domain enumeration\n    is imposed on bound data.\n  accounts:\n    source: CVACT01Y\n    length: 300\n    key: [accountId]\n    fields:\n      - {name: accountId, picture: '9(11)', length: 11}\n      - {name: activeStatus, picture: 'X(01)', length: 1}\n      - {name: currentBalance, picture: 'S9(10)V99', length: 12}\n      - {name: creditLimit, picture: 'S9(10)V99', length: 12}\n      - {name: cashCreditLimit, picture: 'S9(10)V99', length: 12}\n      - {name: openDate, picture: 'X(10)', length: 10}\n      - {name: expirationDate, picture: 'X(10)', length: 10}\n      - {name: reissueDate, picture: 'X(10)', length: 10}\n      - {name: currentCycleCredit, picture: 'S9(10)V99', length: 12}\n      - {name: currentCycleDebit, picture: 'S9(10)V99', length: 12}\n      - {name: addressZip, picture: 'X(10)', length: 10}\n      - {name: groupId, picture: 'X(10)', length: 10}\n      - {name: filler, picture: 'X(178)', length: 178}\n  cardCrossReference:\n    source: CVACT03Y\n    length: 50\n    key: [cardNumber]\n    interestAlternateKey: [accountId]\n    fields:\n      - {name: cardNumber, picture: 'X(16)', length: 16}\n      - {name: customerId, picture: '9(09)', length: 9}\n      - {name: accountId, picture: '9(11)', length: 11}\n      - {name: filler, picture: 'X(14)', length: 14}\n  categoryBalances:\n    source: CVTRA01Y\n    length: 50\n    key: [accountId, typeCode, categoryCode]\n    fields:\n      - {name: accountId, picture: '9(11)', length: 11}\n      - {name: typeCode, picture: 'X(02)', length: 2}\n      - {name: categoryCode, picture: '9(04)', length: 4}\n      - {name: balance, picture: 'S9(09)V99', length: 11}\n      - {name: filler, picture: 'X(22)', length: 22}\n  disclosureGroups:\n    source: CVTRA02Y\n    length: 50\n    key: [groupId, typeCode, categoryCode]\n    fields:\n      - {name: groupId, picture: 'X(10)', length: 10}\n      - {name: typeCode, picture: 'X(02)', length: 2}\n      - {name: categoryCode, picture: '9(04)', length: 4}\n      - {name: interestRate, picture: 'S9(04)V99', length: 6}\n      - {name: filler, picture: 'X(28)', length: 28}\n  transactionTypes:\n    source: CVTRA03Y\n    length: 60\n    key: [typeCode]\n    fields:\n      - {name: typeCode, picture: 'X(02)', length: 2}\n      - {name: description, picture: 'X(50)', length: 50}\n      - {name: filler, picture: 'X(08)', length: 8}\n  transactionCategories:\n    source: CVTRA04Y\n    length: 60\n    key: [typeCode, categoryCode]\n    fields:\n      - {name: typeCode, picture: 'X(02)', length: 2}\n      - {name: categoryCode, picture: '9(04)', length: 4}\n      - {name: description, picture: 'X(50)', length: 50}\n      - {name: filler, picture: 'X(04)', length: 4}\n"},"sequence_number":6435}

event: response.output_item.done
data: {"type":"response.output_item.done","item":{"id":"msg_014ad5a681765dc9016aa3e748bfa087d2afcd55daab953c60","type":"message","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"output_text","annotations":[],"logprobs":[],"text":"openapi: 3.1.0\ninfo:\n  title: CardDemo Batch Transaction Boundary\n  version: 1.0.0\n  description: |\n    Contract for individual invocations of CBTRN02C (posting), CBACT04C\n    (interest generation), and CBTRN03C (reporting), not for an entire batch\n    schedule.\n\n    HTTP paths, synchronous POST requests, JSON envelopes, dataset binding\n    identifiers, base64 record transport, and HTTP status codes are chosen\n    transport conventions. They are not interfaces implemented by the COBOL\n    sources. A dataset binding identifies an already provisioned file in the\n    execution environment; it does not create or validate its contents.\n\n    Sequential input records are supplied in order. Persistent indexed files\n    are accessed through bindings with the access modes described per operation.\n    Output arrays expose logical records written by the program, without\n    sequential-file block headers or record framing. They do not imply that\n    output files or writes are transactional. Missing keys, duplicate transaction\n    identifiers, arbitrary alphanumeric dates and card numbers, empty files,\n    and malformed numeric storage remain representable.\n\n    All three programs display diagnostics and call CEE3ABD with code 999 and\n    timing 0 on their explicit abend paths. Availability and actual behavior of\n    that external routine are not established by the corpus. No atomicity,\n    rollback, retry, idempotency, locking, or automatic recovery is promised.\n    Earlier writes and output-file initialization may persist after failure.\nx-uncertainties:\n  - The corpus supplies no HTTP server, runtime deployment, encoding configuration, or proof that the referenced datasets and utilities are available.\n  - Raw records use the execution environment's COBOL display encoding, including signed display numeric representation. This contract does not prescribe ASCII, EBCDIC, or a sign-overpunch translation.\n  - COBOL arithmetic has fixed receiving-field sizes and no ON SIZE ERROR handling here. Overflow and malformed numeric data are not converted into invented business rejections.\n  - SORT, IDCAMS, CEE3ABD, and the REPROCT control member are not supplied implementations. JCL references do not establish their execution.\n  - TRANBKP describes backup, deletion, and redefinition of the transaction master. COMBTRAN describes sorting backup plus system transactions by ID and loading the master. Neither is implicitly executed by these operations.\n  - TRANREPT JCL describes external unload, date filtering, and card-number sorting. These steps are not implicitly executed by the reporting operation; the JCL also repeats the STEP05R step name.\npaths:\n  /transaction-postings:\n    post:\n      operationId: postDailyTransactions\n      summary: Run daily transaction posting\n      description: |\n        Executes the observable boundary of CBTRN02C. DALYTRAN is read\n        sequentially; XREFFILE is input; ACCTFILE and TCATBALF are I-O.\n        TRANFILE is indexed with a 16-byte transaction-ID key and is opened\n        OUTPUT, not I-O or EXTEND. DALYREJS is opened OUTPUT. This is not an\n        append-to-existing-master promise; output initialization can replace\n        existing content according to the runtime.\n\n        Each successfully read daily record increments the processed counter.\n        Validation first reads the card cross-reference. INVALID KEY gives\n        0100, INVALID CARD NUMBER FOUND. Only if that succeeds is the account\n        read; INVALID KEY gives 0101, ACCOUNT RECORD NOT FOUND. With an account,\n        a signed nine-integer-digit, two-decimal temporary value is computed as\n        currentCycleCredit - currentCycleDebit + dailyAmount. A value greater\n        than creditLimit gives 0102, OVERLIMIT TRANSACTION. Then expirationDate\n        is compared as PIC X(10) to the first ten characters of originalTimestamp.\n        If expirationDate is less, 0103, TRANSACTION RECEIVED AFTER ACCT\n        EXPIRATION, overwrites 0102. Equality passes both comparisons.\n\n        A rejected record is copied unchanged, including its processing timestamp\n        and filler, to a 430-byte rejection record with a four-digit reason and\n        a space-padded 76-character message. Processing continues. Rejected\n        records do not take the posting branch. A completed run with any\n        rejections explicitly sets RETURN-CODE to 4. The no-rejection branch\n        does not explicitly assign RETURN-CODE.\n\n        Posting copies all named transaction fields except processingTimestamp,\n        which is replaced by the runtime current timestamp. Filler is not copied\n        or initialized explicitly. Effects occur in this order:\n        (1) read category balance by account, type, category; on status 23 create\n        an initialized balance record containing the amount, otherwise add the\n        amount and rewrite;\n        (2) add amount to account currentBalance; if amount >= 0 add it to\n        currentCycleCredit, otherwise add the negative amount to\n        currentCycleDebit; rewrite the account;\n        (3) write the indexed transaction record.\n\n        Account rewrite INVALID KEY sets internal reason 0109, ACCOUNT RECORD\n        NOT FOUND, but that value is not retested for rejection and does not\n        increment the reject counter. The transaction write is still attempted.\n        No separate 0109 rejection response is promised. Other statuses on\n        validation lookups and account rewrite are not comprehensively checked.\n\n        Checked open/close failures, daily read statuses other than 00/10,\n        category read statuses other than 00/23, category write/rewrite failures,\n        rejection writes, and transaction writes lead to the explicit abend path.\n        A duplicate transaction key can fail the final write after balance\n        changes; there is no duplicate prevalidation. No card-number digit or\n        checksum validation, account-active validation, cash-limit validation,\n        transaction type/category lookup, positivity restriction, or calendar\n        validation is present.\n      x-preconditions:\n        - Bound files must be provisioned in the environment with the declared organization and access permissions.\n        - XREFFILE uses the 16-byte card key; ACCTFILE uses the 11-digit account key; TCATBALF uses the 17-byte account/type/category key.\n        - Input order is significant because accepted records update balances used by later records.\n      requestBody:\n        required: true\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              type: object\n              additionalProperties: false\n              required:\n                - dailyTransactions\n                - cardCrossReference\n                - accounts\n                - categoryBalances\n                - transactionOutput\n                - rejectionOutput\n              properties:\n                dailyTransactions:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/TransactionRecords'\n                cardCrossReference:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n                accounts:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n                categoryBalances:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n                transactionOutput:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n                rejectionOutput:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: Completed invocation, including completion with business rejections.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                allOf:\n                  - $ref: '#/components/schemas/CompletedRun'\n                  - type: object\n                    required: [processedCount, rejectedCount, transactionsWritten, rejections]\n                    properties:\n                      processedCount:\n                        $ref: '#/components/schemas/Counter'\n                      rejectedCount:\n                        $ref: '#/components/schemas/Counter'\n                      transactionsWritten:\n                        $ref: '#/components/schemas/TransactionRecords'\n                      rejections:\n                        type: array\n                        items:\n                          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Rejection'\n        '500':\n          $ref: '#/components/responses/ExecutionFailure'\n  /interest-transaction-generations:\n    post:\n      operationId: generateInterestTransactions\n      summary: Generate system interest transactions from category balances\n      description: |\n        Executes CBACT04C independently of posting and master-combination jobs.\n        TCATBALF is indexed sequential input in account/type/category key order.\n        XREFFILE and DISCGRP are random input, ACCTFILE is random I-O, and\n        TRANSACT is sequential OUTPUT. No indexed transaction master is written.\n\n        On each account change, the prior account is rewritten, except before\n        the first account. The program then resets its accumulated interest,\n        reads the new account, and reads the cross-reference using the alternate\n        account-ID key. It uses the returned card number, not a caller-selected\n        card. Account or cross-reference read failure abends.\n\n        For every category balance it reads the disclosure rate using the account\n        group, balance type, and balance category. Status 23 causes another read\n        with group DEFAULT padded to ten characters, retaining type and category.\n        Failure of that default read abends; other nonzero initial read statuses\n        except 23 also abend.\n\n        When rate is nonzero, monthlyInterest = balance * rate / 1200 is assigned\n        to PIC S9(09)V99 without ROUNDED, and added to a same-sized account\n        accumulator. One transaction is written even if the calculated interest\n        is zero or negative. A zero rate writes no transaction. Fee calculation\n        is a no-op.\n\n        The transaction ID is the ten-character parameter followed by a six-digit\n        counter starting at 000001, incremented for each generated transaction.\n        The parameter length field is not inspected and the parameter is not\n        validated as a date. Type is 01, numeric category is 0005, source is\n        System padded to ten characters, description begins 'Int. for a/c '\n        followed by the eleven-digit account ID, amount is monthlyInterest,\n        merchant ID is zero, and merchant name/city/ZIP are spaces.\n        Both timestamps are runtime current timestamps. Transaction working\n        storage is not initialized per write; description tail and filler are\n        not explicitly assigned.\n\n        Updating an account adds accumulated interest to currentBalance and\n        sets both cycle credit and cycle debit to zero. Critically, the source\n        performs this update on transition to another account only. The ELSE\n        intended to update at EOF is unreachable under the loop condition:\n        EOF is set by the read while already inside the other branch. Consequently\n        the final account is not rewritten, even though its generated\n        transactions may be written. An empty balance file rewrites no accounts.\n        Category balances are input-only and are not cleared or updated.\n\n        Checked open/close, sequential read other than EOF, lookup, account\n        rewrite, and transaction write failures invoke the abend path. Generated\n        transactions are not automatically posted, merged, or loaded.\n      x-preconditions:\n        - TCATBALF must support sequential indexed-key traversal.\n        - XREFFILE must support the account-ID alternate-key read used by this program.\n        - INTCALC JCL references XREFFIL1 as an alternate-index path, but availability and association of that infrastructure are not established.\n      x-uncertainties:\n        - Behavior of six-digit transaction suffix overflow is not handled explicitly; generated IDs are not checked for collisions.\n        - Multiple cross-reference rows for an account and runtime alternate-index behavior are not resolved by the supplied source.\n      requestBody:\n        required: true\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              type: object\n              additionalProperties: false\n              required:\n                - transactionIdPrefix\n                - categoryBalances\n                - cardCrossReference\n                - accounts\n                - disclosureGroups\n                - transactionOutput\n              properties:\n                transactionIdPrefix:\n                  type: string\n                  minLength: 10\n                  maxLength: 10\n                  description: |\n                    Exact PIC X(10) linkage parameter, mapped to ten execution-encoding\n                    bytes. Not an ISO date. INTCALC supplies 2022071800.\n                  examples: ['2022071800', 'XXXXXXXXXX']\n                categoryBalances:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n                cardCrossReference:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n                accounts:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n                disclosureGroups:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n                transactionOutput:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: |\n            Completed generation. Account rewrites are limited to account\n            transitions as described, not all accounts represented in output.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                allOf:\n                  - $ref: '#/components/schemas/CompletedRun'\n                  - type: object\n                    required: [transactionsWritten]\n                    properties:\n                      transactionsWritten:\n                        $ref: '#/components/schemas/TransactionRecords'\n        '500':\n          $ref: '#/components/responses/ExecutionFailure'\n  /transaction-reports:\n    post:\n      operationId: generateTransactionReport\n      summary: Produce the fixed-width daily transaction detail report\n      description: |\n        Executes CBTRN03C against the supplied sequential transaction stream.\n        CARDXREF, TRANTYPE, and TRANCATG are indexed random input. TRANREPT is\n        sequential OUTPUT. This operation changes no input master records.\n\n        Only the first DATEPARM record is read: positions 1-10 are startDate,\n        position 11 is ignored, and positions 12-21 are endDate. Remaining bytes\n        and subsequent records are ignored. An empty DATEPARM file sets EOF and\n        skips transaction processing, leaving the opened output without report\n        records. Dates are unvalidated PIC X(10); no start-before-end validation\n        is performed.\n\n        The first ten characters of processingTimestamp are compared inclusively\n        against the date parameters. A failed comparison uses NEXT SENTENCE,\n        skipping the remainder of the main processing sentence for that iteration.\n        Records are neither sorted nor regrouped internally.\n\n        On a change of card number among included records, a prior 'Account Total'\n        is printed if details have begun, then the new card cross-reference is\n        read. Thus grouping is by contiguous card, not by account ID. Each included\n        record looks up its type and its type/category pair. INVALID KEY on these\n        three lookups displays the offending key, reports status 23, and abends.\n        Other lookup statuses are not comprehensively checked. Blank initial card\n        numbers can bypass the first cross-reference lookup because the current\n        card working field initially contains spaces.\n\n        The first detail causes four header lines. Before each detail, a page\n        break is considered only if lineCounter MOD 20 = 0. The counter includes\n        headers, details, totals and separator lines; it is not reset per page.\n        A page-total routine writes its total and a hyphen separator, adds the\n        page total to the grand total, resets the page total, and increments\n        the counter twice. An account-total routine writes its total and a\n        separator, resets the account total, and also increments it twice.\n\n        At transaction EOF the program still evaluates the date condition on\n        transaction working storage. If that condition passes, the EOF branch\n        adds TRAN-AMT again to page and account accumulators, writes page totals,\n        then grand totals. It does not write the final account total. With the\n        usual retained last record this double-counts the last amount in final\n        page/grand totals. If the retained last record is out of range, NEXT\n        SENTENCE skips final totals. Empty transaction input leaves these tests\n        dependent on uninitialized transaction storage. This contract does not\n        substitute corrected totals or guarantee an empty-input grand-total line.\n\n        Checked open/close failures, transaction/date reads other than 00/10,\n        report writes, and invalid lookup keys take the explicit abend path.\n      x-preconditions:\n        - The caller must provide the desired sequential stream; contiguous card ordering is needed for consolidated card subtotals but is not validated or enforced.\n        - External JCL filtering uses independently hard-coded dates 2022-01-01 through 2022-07-06 and sorts the card field as ZD. Those constraints are not restrictions on this program-level input.\n      requestBody:\n        required: true\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              type: object\n              additionalProperties: false\n              required:\n                - transactions\n                - dateParameterRecords\n                - cardCrossReference\n                - transactionTypes\n                - transactionCategories\n                - reportOutput\n              properties:\n                transactions:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/TransactionRecords'\n                dateParameterRecords:\n                  type: array\n                  description: Empty is permitted; only the first record is read.\n                  items:\n                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/DateParameterRecord'\n                cardCrossReference:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n                transactionTypes:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n                transactionCategories:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n                reportOutput:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/DatasetBinding'\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: Completed report, preserving the source formatting and control-flow behavior.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                allOf:\n                  - $ref: '#/components/schemas/CompletedRun'\n                  - type: object\n                    required: [reportRecords]\n                    properties:\n                      reportRecords:\n                        type: array\n                        items:\n                          $ref: '#/components/schemas/ReportRecord'\n        '500':\n          $ref: '#/components/responses/ExecutionFailure'\ncomponents:\n  responses:\n    ExecutionFailure:\n      description: |\n        Transport convention for an invocation that does not complete normally.\n        This is distinct from a posting business rejection. Diagnostics and\n        partial output are exposed only if recoverable from the execution\n        environment. No reversal of output initialization or earlier writes is\n        implied. A close failure can occur after all record effects.\n      content:\n        application/json:\n          schema:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/FailedRun'\n  schemas:\n    DatasetBinding:\n      type: string\n      minLength: 1\n      description: |\n        Opaque transport identifier for a pre-existing runtime file binding.\n        Missing, inaccessible, incorrectly organized, or incorrectly provisioned\n        resources are execution failures, not exclusions from this schema.\n        No public dataset-management operation is defined.\n    Counter:\n      type: integer\n      minimum: 0\n      maximum: 999999999\n      description: Value of the program's nine-digit counter, not an unlimited count.\n    CompletedRun:\n      type: object\n      required: [outcome, diagnostics]\n      properties:\n        outcome:\n          const: completed\n        returnCode:\n          type: integer\n          description: |\n            Runtime return code if available. Posting explicitly sets 4 when\n            any records were rejected; otherwise these programs do not explicitly\n            establish a success return code.\n        diagnostics:\n          type: array\n          items:\n            type: string\n          description: DISPLAY output in execution order, decoded by the environment.\n    FailedRun:\n      type: object\n      required: [outcome, diagnostics]\n      properties:\n        outcome:\n          const: failed\n        program:\n          type: string\n          enum: [CBTRN02C, CBACT04C, CBTRN03C]\n        diagnostics:\n          type: array\n          items:\n            type: string\n        abendCode:\n          type: integer\n          const: 999\n          description: Present when the explicit CEE3ABD request is observed.\n        fileStatus:\n          type: string\n          description: |\n            Observed file-status diagnostic, when available; not normalized into\n            a business error. The programs expand nonnumeric or 9-prefixed status\n            values using a binary second byte. Posting's rejection-file close\n            failure mistakenly displays XREFFILE status.\n        partialTransactions:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/TransactionRecords'\n        partialRejections:\n          type: array\n          items:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/Rejection'\n        partialReportRecords:\n          type: array\n          items:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/ReportRecord'\n        effectsDescription:\n          type: string\n          description: Observed effects only; omission does not establish that no writes persisted.\n    TransactionRecords:\n      type: array\n      description: |\n        Logical 350-byte records in input or write order. Empty arrays, repeated\n        identifiers, nonnumeric card numbers, arbitrary timestamps, negative\n        amounts and raw malformed numeric storage are representable.\n      items:\n        $ref: '#/components/schemas/TransactionRecord'\n    TransactionRecord:\n      type: string\n      contentEncoding: base64\n      contentMediaType: application/octet-stream\n      x-decoded-byte-length: 350\n      description: |\n        Exactly 350 decoded bytes, CVTRA05Y or CVTRA06Y. Widths and offsets\n        below are one-based, in bytes, with no delimiters. Raw transport retains\n        filler and invalid display-numeric bytes rather than introducing\n        unsupported field validation. Numeric pictures describe intended storage,\n        not business admissibility. Signed values use the runtime display sign\n        representation, without an extra sign byte. V is an implied decimal.\n\n        Named fields on accepted postings are copied except processingTimestamp;\n        rejection output preserves the entire original record. Runtime-generated\n        timestamps have the form YYYY-MM-DD-HH.MM.SS.hh0000, with hundredths from\n        CURRENT-DATE and no timezone suffix; they are not RFC 3339.\n      x-record-layout:\n        - {name: transactionId, offset: 1, length: 16, picture: 'X(16)'}\n        - {name: typeCode, offset: 17, length: 2, picture: 'X(02)'}\n        - {name: categoryCode, offset: 19, length: 4, picture: '9(04)'}\n        - {name: source, offset: 23, length: 10, picture: 'X(10)'}\n        - {name: description, offset: 33, length: 100, picture: 'X(100)'}\n        - {name: amount, offset: 133, length: 11, picture: 'S9(09)V99', nominalRange: '-999999999.99 to 999999999.99'}\n        - {name: merchantId, offset: 144, length: 9, picture: '9(09)'}\n        - {name: merchantName, offset: 153, length: 50, picture: 'X(50)'}\n        - {name: merchantCity, offset: 203, length: 50, picture: 'X(50)'}\n        - {name: merchantZip, offset: 253, length: 10, picture: 'X(10)'}\n        - {name: cardNumber, offset: 263, length: 16, picture: 'X(16)'}\n        - {name: originalTimestamp, offset: 279, length: 26, picture: 'X(26)'}\n        - {name: processingTimestamp, offset: 305, length: 26, picture: 'X(26)'}\n        - {name: filler, offset: 331, length: 20, picture: 'X(20)'}\n    Rejection:\n      type: object\n      required: [record, reasonCode, reasonDescription]\n      properties:\n        record:\n          type: string\n          contentEncoding: base64\n          contentMediaType: application/octet-stream\n          x-decoded-byte-length: 430\n          description: |\n            Original 350-byte daily transaction followed by PIC 9(04) reason\n            and PIC X(76) description, space-padded.\n        reasonCode:\n          type: string\n          enum: ['0100', '0101', '0102', '0103']\n        reasonDescription:\n          type: string\n          enum:\n            - INVALID CARD NUMBER FOUND\n            - ACCOUNT RECORD NOT FOUND\n            - OVERLIMIT TRANSACTION\n            - TRANSACTION RECEIVED AFTER ACCT EXPIRATION\n      description: Decoded reason fields are transport projections of the raw trailer, with trailing message spaces removed.\n    DateParameterRecord:\n      type: string\n      contentEncoding: base64\n      contentMediaType: application/octet-stream\n      x-decoded-byte-length: 80\n      description: |\n        Exactly 80 decoded bytes. Start date is bytes 1-10, byte 11 is ignored,\n        end date is bytes 12-21, bytes 22-80 are ignored. Arbitrary character\n        content, reversed ranges, and spaces are representable; there is no\n        calendar or separator validation.\n    ReportRecord:\n      type: string\n      contentEncoding: base64\n      contentMediaType: application/octet-stream\n      x-decoded-byte-length: 133\n      description: |\n        Exactly 133 decoded bytes, including trailing spaces. CVTRA07Y headers\n        name DALYREPT and Daily Transaction Report and contain Date Range with\n        the supplied start/end strings. Detail columns contain transaction ID\n        (16), space, account ID (11), space, type (2), hyphen, type description\n        truncated to 15, space, category (4), hyphen, category description\n        truncated to 29, space, source (10), four spaces, amount edited with\n        PIC -ZZZ,ZZZ,ZZZ.ZZ, and two spaces, then padding to 133.\n        Separators contain 133 hyphens. Page Total, Account Total and Grand\n        Total lines have dotted leaders and PIC +ZZZ,ZZZ,ZZZ.ZZ values.\n        Report totals are source accumulators, not independently recomputed\n        or corrected API aggregates.\nx-persistent-record-layouts:\n  description: |\n    Layout evidence for datasets referenced by DatasetBinding. These are not\n    new provisioning or maintenance APIs. Keys retain leading zeros and fixed\n    character padding. No foreign-key completeness or business-domain enumeration\n    is imposed on bound data.\n  accounts:\n    source: CVACT01Y\n    length: 300\n    key: [accountId]\n    fields:\n      - {name: accountId, picture: '9(11)', length: 11}\n      - {name: activeStatus, picture: 'X(01)', length: 1}\n      - {name: currentBalance, picture: 'S9(10)V99', length: 12}\n      - {name: creditLimit, picture: 'S9(10)V99', length: 12}\n      - {name: cashCreditLimit, picture: 'S9(10)V99', length: 12}\n      - {name: openDate, picture: 'X(10)', length: 10}\n      - {name: expirationDate, picture: 'X(10)', length: 10}\n      - {name: reissueDate, picture: 'X(10)', length: 10}\n      - {name: currentCycleCredit, picture: 'S9(10)V99', length: 12}\n      - {name: currentCycleDebit, picture: 'S9(10)V99', length: 12}\n      - {name: addressZip, picture: 'X(10)', length: 10}\n      - {name: groupId, picture: 'X(10)', length: 10}\n      - {name: filler, picture: 'X(178)', length: 178}\n  cardCrossReference:\n    source: CVACT03Y\n    length: 50\n    key: [cardNumber]\n    interestAlternateKey: [accountId]\n    fields:\n      - {name: cardNumber, picture: 'X(16)', length: 16}\n      - {name: customerId, picture: '9(09)', length: 9}\n      - {name: accountId, picture: '9(11)', length: 11}\n      - {name: filler, picture: 'X(14)', length: 14}\n  categoryBalances:\n    source: CVTRA01Y\n    length: 50\n    key: [accountId, typeCode, categoryCode]\n    fields:\n      - {name: accountId, picture: '9(11)', length: 11}\n      - {name: typeCode, picture: 'X(02)', length: 2}\n      - {name: categoryCode, picture: '9(04)', length: 4}\n      - {name: balance, picture: 'S9(09)V99', length: 11}\n      - {name: filler, picture: 'X(22)', length: 22}\n  disclosureGroups:\n    source: CVTRA02Y\n    length: 50\n    key: [groupId, typeCode, categoryCode]\n    fields:\n      - {name: groupId, picture: 'X(10)', length: 10}\n      - {name: typeCode, picture: 'X(02)', length: 2}\n      - {name: categoryCode, picture: '9(04)', length: 4}\n      - {name: interestRate, picture: 'S9(04)V99', length: 6}\n      - {name: filler, picture: 'X(28)', length: 28}\n  transactionTypes:\n    source: CVTRA03Y\n    length: 60\n    key: [typeCode]\n    fields:\n      - {name: typeCode, picture: 'X(02)', length: 2}\n      - {name: description, picture: 'X(50)', length: 50}\n      - {name: filler, picture: 'X(08)', length: 8}\n  transactionCategories:\n    source: CVTRA04Y\n    length: 60\n    key: [typeCode, categoryCode]\n    fields:\n      - {name: typeCode, picture: 'X(02)', length: 2}\n      - {name: categoryCode, picture: '9(04)', length: 4}\n      - {name: description, picture: 'X(50)', length: 50}\n      - {name: filler, picture: 'X(04)', length: 4}\n"}],"phase":"final_answer","role":"assistant"},"output_index":1,"sequence_number":6436}

